    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "1985095199153176948",
      "url": "https://x.com/southcoastwx/status/1985095199153176948",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/southcoastwx/status/1985095199153176948",
      "text": "❗️Damaging winds and heavy rainfall is expected over the Central Phillipines amid the landfall of typhoon Kalmaegi Monday night❗️\n\nForecasts by region for the Phillipines: \n\nEastern Visayas: \nTyphoon conditions are expected from 7:00 pm Monday evening until 8:00 am Tuesday over southern sections. \nHazards: \n• Wind gusts: 120 to 140km/h except locally up to 190km/h near Suluan. Winds will be less severe over northern sections. \n• Rainfall amounts: 50 to 100 mm except locally more then 200 mm over southern sections\n\nCentral Visayas: \nTyphoon conditions are possible from 1:00 am until 9:00 am Tuesday. \nHazards: \n• Wind gusts 100 to 130km/h except locally 150km/h over northern sections\n• Rainfall amounts: 150 to 250 mm\n\nWestern Visayas:\nTyphoon conditions are expected from 7 am Tuesday until 7:00 pm. \n\nHazards: \n• Wind gusts: 120 to 140km/h except 150 to 170km/h over exposed shores\n• Rainfall amounts 150 to 250 mm over southern sections, 50 to 100 mm over northern sections. \n\nMimaropa: \nTyphoon conditions are possible over northern sections from 11:00 pm Tuesday until 7:00 am Wednesday. \nHazards: \n• Wind gusts: Up to 140km/h over northern sections \n• Rainfall amounts: Up to 350 mm over northern sections\n\nFor the remainder of the central Phillipines, heavy rainfall and tropical storm force winds are expected at times Monday night into Tuesday night, beginning and ending a bit later over the western sections. \nThose located in the Visayas regions are advised to be prepared for destructive wind gusts locally ranging 150 to 200km/h Monday night. \nSevere flooding is possible locally and landslides are expected in areas of steep terrain. \nConsider moving to a storm shelter, especially over the southeastern Visayas coast. Prepare for evacuation orders. \n\nThe next forecast will be posted by 12:30 pm Phillipines time today. \n\nKalmaegi is forecast to exit the Philippines  Tuesday night, and the storm is expected to intensify into a T5 storm, possibly even reaching T6 status, with sustained winds 190-220km/h. \n\nBoth the North and the South Central Coast Regions of Vietnam are advised to postpone travel plans for Nov 6-7th. \n\nPlease stay updated on the most recent forecasts. #Typhoon #Phillipines #TyphoonKalmaegi #Storm #Vietnam",
